      "id": "rdls_exp-ken_rcmrd_housingmaterialstonemud",
      "title": "Housing Material_Stone with Mud",
      "description": "Data on houses whose main material is made of stone with mud. Housing materials are part of the Population and Housing indicators in DHS, used to assess household living standards, wealth index composition, and environmental health conditions.The DHS records materials for floors, walls, and roofs. Stone with mud falls under category two of Rudimentary Materials. They represent an intermediate level - locally made or partially processed materials, often transitional between poor and durable housing and reflects modest or semi-permanent structures; common in peri-urban settings. [Source: This metadata record was automatically extracted from the GeoNode portal rcmrd]",
